Azure Cloud Administration

Azure Cloud Administration Lab Portfolio – Overview
This project demonstrates hands on experience with core services in Microsoft Azure through a series of practical labs designed to simulate real world IT support and cloud administration scenarios. The labs focus on infrastructure deployment, networking configuration, security access control, monitoring, and storage management within a cloud environment.
The goal of these exercises is to build and troubleshoot common situations that cloud administrators and IT support engineers encounter when managing virtual infrastructure in Azure.
Lab Areas Covered


## Lab 1 – Azure Infrastructure Deployment ##
 Creating a Resource Group and deploying a Virtual Machine. Configure a Azure Virtual Machines instance, apply a Azure Network Security Group, and connecting to it using RDP to validate connectivity. 

## Lab 2 – RDP Connectivity Troubleshooting ##
 Simulate an access failure by misconfiguring a Network Security Group rule that blocks RDP traffic. And then  using Azure Network Watcher to investigate inbound connectivity and correct the issue.

## Lab 3 – RBAC Permission Configuration ##
 Creating a test user and simulating an access restriction scenario. Resolve the issue by assigning the appropriate role using Role-Based Access Control 

## Lab 4 – VM Monitoring and Performance Investigation ## 
 Using Azure Monitor to review system metrics, investigate VM health, and analyze logs to troubleshoot a performance related issues

## Lab 5 – Web Server Deployment with Network Security Controls ##
 Deploying a simple web server on a virtual machine and allowing HTTP traffic through port 80 using an NSG rule. Apply IP restrictions to demonstrate network security best practices.

## Lab 6 – Cloud Storage Configuration ##
 Create a storage account and configure containers using Azure Blob Storage. Implement access controls such as RBAC and SAS tokens to demonstrate secure data access management.
